diagnosis_text:
- Affected component: The HTTPS (TLS) service layer on the web servers is not running/listening. Specifically, Apache on web_server_2 and web_server_3 has no SSL/443 listener configured.
- Mechanism: The user’s browser likely attempts HTTPS by default (HTTPS-First behavior or bookmark/protocol auto-upgrade). TCP connections to 10.200.0.5:443 (web2.local) and 10.200.0.6:443 (web3.local) are refused by the host stack, so the page “spins” and then fails to load, while plain HTTP works.
- Localization: Application layer on web_server_2 and web_server_3. Evidence:
  • From host_1_1_1_1: curl http://web2.local and http://web3.local return HTTP/1.1 200 OK immediately.
  • From host_1_1_1_1: curl -vk http
